WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
On the Home screen, click Open project… and choose the project of the tutorial Repair instead of cropping.

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.000
The project opens up to date: nothing is to be computed.

3
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:11.000
Click Post.

4
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:19.000
Before any gesture: a veil on the sky, the ring a little pale, the fine structure soft at full size. The Version list holds Version 1.

5
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Double-click the name of the version, type Whole field and press Enter: this is the picture as it is, for a screen view.

6
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.000
The first version is named Whole field.

7
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:33.000
Click New version: a copy of this one, with its own Undo.

8
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:37.000
Rename it Finish, the version for full size.

9
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Click Starless image.

10
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.000
Click Filter, open Contrast and choose Dehaze.

11
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Drag Amount to about 0.25 and Scale to about 256 px.

12
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:52.000
With the filter selected, click the mask button, then Add to mask and Luminance range.

13
00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:57.000
Set the part to 0 to 25 % with a Feather of about 8 px: Dehaze acts on the dark tones only.

14
00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:01.000
Click Filter, open Color and choose Saturation: drag Strength to about +20 %.

15
00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:05.000
Click Filter, open Detail and choose Multiscale sharpening.

16
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:09.000
Raise 4 px to 0.3, 8 px to 0.4 and 16 px to 0.3; leave 1 px and 2 px at 0.

17
00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:13.000
Open the Version list: two versions.

18
00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:18.000
Pick Whole field: the picture changes at once, with its own settings.

19
00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:22.000
Pick Finish again.

20
00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:27.000
Click Undo: it takes back the last change of this version only, here the 16 px value.

21
00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:31.000
Click Redo to bring it back.

22
00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:36.000
Click the bin: the version shown is deleted, and Ctrl+Z offers it back.

23
00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:40.000
Press Ctrl+Z: the version comes back with its settings.

24
00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:44.000
With Finish shown, click Export… and write a first file.

25
00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:48.000
Pick Whole field and export the second file.

26
00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:51.000
Each version has its own file.

27
00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:55.000
Press Ctrl+S: both versions are saved with the project.

28
00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:58.000
Open File, then click Close project.

29
00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:01.000
Click the project to open it again.

30
00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:07.000
Both versions are still in the list, each with its settings.
